{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Because that, etc., and he atoned, etc.</b> He gave the reason why YHWH chose to privilege Phinehas with the priesthood by way of a gift from HaShem, and not by the power of his father — He said <b>because he was zealous for his Elohim</b>: he acted for his Elohim and was zealous for His honor; so his Elohim too would exalt him without his needing to benefit in his prestige from his father's prestige. And corresponding to what He said that there would be peace for him and also for his seed etc., He said <b>and he atoned for the children of Israel</b> — meaning, that he made peace between Israel and their Father in heaven, and delivered Israel from the wrath of the king, the angel of death; therefore the covenant of peace would be his from them. And just as the benefit he bestowed through his atonement for the children of Israel is a benefit that endures — for every generation that comes exists by virtue of the first ones upon whom he atoned — therefore likewise his benefaction would also endure, and it would be his and his seed after him, a covenant of everlasting priesthood." "<b>And by way of</b> remez (hint), it is explained according to the words of the Sages, whose memory is for blessing (Numbers Rabbah 21:3), who said: Phinehas is Elijah, who is destined to bring tidings to the people of Israel in the final exile. And here Scripture informs us through what he merited this exalted level — to turn the heart of the children back to their fathers. And they said, whose memory is for blessing (Eduyot 8:7): Elijah comes only to increase peace in the world. And this is the verse's saying <b>Phinehas</b> etc. <b>turned back</b> etc. <b>in his zeal</b> etc. — it repeated to say two instances of zeal, to allude to the zeal he displayed at this time and to the zeal he displayed a second time in the days of Ahab, as it says (1 Kings 19:14): ״קַנֹּא קִנֵּאתִי לַה׳״. There too it repeated to say ״קַנֹּא קִנֵּאתִי״ to allude to two acts of zeal: one in the days of Moses and one in the days of Ahab." "Therefore He said <b>Behold, I give him My covenant of peace</b> — which is the covenant He made with the fathers to give them the ten nations, and this is called the covenant of peace because then there will be peace in all the world, as it is written (Isaiah 11:7): ״וּפָרָה וָדֹב תִּרְעֶינָה״ etc. ״לֹא יָרֵעוּ וְלֹא יַשְׁחִיתוּ״ etc. This covenant would be his, for he is the one who will do this thing and turn the heart of the children back to their fathers etc., as it is written (Malachi 3:23): ״הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי שֹׁלֵחַ לָכֶם אֶת אֵלִיָּה״ etc. And therefore the verse was precise in saying <b>Behold, I give him</b> specifically, and did not include his seed with him. And afterward He said the covenant of priesthood: ״וְהָיְתָה לּוֹ וּלְזַרְעוֹ אַחֲרָיו בְּרִית כְּהֻנַּת עוֹלָם״. And He concluded by saying <b>because</b> — meaning, these two promises correspond to the two things he did: the covenant of peace is <b>because he was zealous for his Elohim</b>; here He alluded to the zeal he displayed in the days of Ahab, because they abandoned Elohim and worshipped idolatry. And this is what the verse was precise in saying <b>for his Elohim</b> — that he was zealous concerning idolatry, about which it is said (Deuteronomy 6:15): ״כִּי אֵל קַנָּא״ etc. — until all the people said (1 Kings 18:39): ״ה׳ הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים״ etc. Therefore he too will bring tidings on that day when YHWH will be one and His name one, which is also the sod of ״ה׳ הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים״." "And His saying <b>and he atoned</b> etc. corresponds to the promise ״וְהָיְתָה לּוֹ״ etc. ״בְּרִית כְּהֻנַּת״ — for this is his portion, that he atoned for the children of Israel; likewise he would always atone for them, along the lines of what it says (Leviticus 4:20): ״וְכִפֶּר עָלָיו הַכֹּהֵן״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "The ten-nations reference: Or HaChaim alludes to the full inheritance of Canaan in the messianic era."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:30.203312651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}